---

import AboutArticle from "../../components/AboutArticle.astro";
import ProductScreenshot from "../../components/ProductScreenshot.astro";
import { getAboutPage } from "../../lib/aboutPages";
import { getAboutPhoto } from "../../lib/aboutPhotos";

const page = getAboutPage("accounts-and-dashboard")!;
const hero = getAboutPhoto("desk-workspace");
---
<AboutArticle
  slug={page.slug}
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  heroImage={hero.image}
  heroAlt={hero.alt}
  heroCaption={hero.caption}
  heroCredit={hero.credit}
  heroCreditHref={hero.sourceUrl}
>
  <p>
    Creating an account unlocks personalization, devices, history, alerts, and optional paid features.
    The signed-in shell keeps property chrome (space switcher, plan, quick links) while pages stay focused:
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard">Overview</a> for risk and trends,
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/live">Live</a> for current readings,
    Devices / Alerts / History / Share for setup and ops.
  </p>

  <ProductScreenshot
    shot="overview-cards"
    caption="Overview nudges you from device connect through freeze setup and live data."
  />

  <h2>Account creation</h2>
  <p>
    Registration uses email and password via Supabase Auth. Password reset and (when enabled in Supabase)
    OAuth providers such as Google, GitHub, or Discord are available from the sign-in page. New users start
    on the Free plan with a default household.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting started checklist</h2>
  <p>
    Until you finish essentials (a device or feed, freeze email, and a test alert) — or dismiss the prompt —
    Overview stays in a calm <strong>first-run</strong> focus: space status and setup CTAs, without the full
    Status strip or Insights cards. A short checklist covers device connect, confirming readings on Live,
    then optional alerts and household invites. When core and optional steps are done, or you dismiss it,
    the checklist hides; use <strong>Show checklist</strong> to bring it back.
  </p>

  <h2>Overview (Simple vs Insights)</h2>
  <p>
    After first-run,
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard">Overview</a> opens with garage/space risk status and a Status strip:
    last reading, sensors, feeds, alerts, freeze hours (with degree-hours), coldest margin above your freeze
    threshold, indoor−outdoor ΔT, probe spread, condensation hours, and feed health when pull feeds exist.
    A <strong>time-to-freeze clock</strong> sits under space status in both Simple and Insights: when this garage,
    shop, or crawlspace is projected to hit your freeze threshold, using the space's lag vs the outdoor forecast.
    Toggle <strong>Insights</strong> for nights-at-risk, week compare, heating insights, door
    and power correlation, motion, battery/RSSI trends, air quality, energy, and flood/level. The 7-day probe
    chart (Simple and Insights) can show humidity % and dew point (°F) when readings include RH; the same
    controls appear on History. Live cards live on
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/live">Live</a>, not Overview.
  </p>
  <ProductScreenshot
    shot="overview-status"
    caption="Status strip: freeze margin, indoor−outdoor ΔT, probe spread, condensation, and feed health."
  />

  <h2>Live readings</h2>
  <p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/live">Live</a> is the signed-in home for current probe cards, outdoor
    weather when enabled, and offline warnings. Prefer Live after ingest or a pull fetch; use Overview for
    freeze risk and trends.
  </p>

  <h2>Devices &amp; sensors</h2>
  <p>
    Under <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/devices">Devices</a>, <strong>Setup</strong> is for connecting
    hardware and <strong>Status</strong> is for health (last seen, battery, RSSI). You can:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Push devices</strong>. ESP/Arduino POSTs JSON to a unique ingest URL. Copy the key from the 30-minute callout; use <strong>Reveal ingest key</strong> or <strong>Rotate key</strong> later. Sensors auto-import on first POST; rename labels on Devices afterward.</li>
    <li><strong>Pull feeds</strong>: <strong>Pull feeds</strong> tab: HTTPS JSON URLs we fetch every 15 minutes. <strong>Save pull setup</strong> auto-imports probe keys; SenML and Home Assistant REST JSON auto-detect when the root is missing.</li>
  </ul>
  <ProductScreenshot
    shot="devices"
    caption="Devices hub: push ingest, pull feeds, Home Assistant, MQTT, and device health."
  />
  <p>
    Step-by-step: <a class="text-link" href="/about/adding-devices">Adding push and pull devices</a>.
    After sensors are mapped, verify ingest (or wait for the next pull), then open
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/live">Live</a> to confirm live values. Payload examples:
    <a class="text-link" href="/about/ingest-and-webhooks">ingest &amp; webhooks</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Display preferences</h2>
  <p>
    Choose whether Live shows probe sensors, outdoor weather, or both. Preferences live in your profile
    metadata and apply immediately after saving under
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/settings">Settings</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>History</h2>
  <p>
    Paginated history lists temperature/humidity snapshots for your household. Filter by feed, probe, and
    date range; clear filters if a query returns no rows. Browsing is included for all signed-in users;
    CSV download requires Member/Pro (or admin). Background collection runs every **15 minutes** on cron (plus successful push ingests). Refreshing Live can also refresh live cards.
  </p>

  <h2>Household activity</h2>
  <p>
    Owners and managers see a <strong>Recent activity</strong> log on
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/household">Household</a> and
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/share/integrations">Share → Integrations</a>
    share links, alert saves, device transfers, and <strong>ingest key reveals</strong> (audited when someone uses Reveal ingest key).
  </p>

  <h2>Alerts</h2>
  <p>
    Start with <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/alerts?tab=settings#alert-section-essentials">Alerts → Essentials</a>
    (freeze °F + email). After your first ingest POST, Devices can also save essentials inline without leaving
    the setup flow. Free plans include email and Discord; Pro unlocks SMS, browser push, and outbound webhooks.
    Enable a channel only when its destination is filled in: incomplete channels are skipped. Use
    <strong>Send test now</strong> to see which channels actually fired.
  </p>
  <ProductScreenshot
    shot="history-chart"
    caption="History curves with freeze line: humidity and dew point overlay when RH is present."
  />

  <h2>Households &amp; share links</h2>
  <p>
    Invite family by email from <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/household">Household</a>. Members share
    devices and history for that household. Every plan includes one
    <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/share/links">family live share link</a> for people without accounts.
    Pro adds broader share scopes (history/metrics), guest expiries, and revoke anytime.
  </p>

  <h2>Plans</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free</strong>, live sensors, devices (limited), history browse, email/Discord alerts, one family live share link.</li>
    <li><strong>Member</strong>. CSV export.</li>
    <li><strong>Pro</strong>: higher device limits, SMS, push, outbound webhooks, expanded share scopes, claims evidence pack.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Upgrade from the Plans card on the dashboard or Alerts page.
  </p>

  <h2>Admin-only tools</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>User manager</strong>: review accounts and grant or revoke admin membership.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact submissions</strong>: read messages from the public contact form.</li>
    <li><strong>Jobs</strong>: operational job visibility when enabled.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Suggested first path</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a class="text-link" href="/register?next=/dashboard/devices">Create an account</a>.</li>
    <li>One-click <strong>Create push device</strong> under <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/devices?view=setup">Devices → Setup</a> (named Workshop probe by default).</li>
    <li>POST a reading: sensors auto-import, then set freeze °F + email on Devices or Essentials and send a test.</li>
    <li>Confirm cards on <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/live">Live</a>, then Overview space status (Status strip and Insights unlock after essentials).</li>
    <li>Optionally invite household members and share a family live link.</li>
  </ol>
</AboutArticle>
